Subject: [PATCH] i2c: atr: backport address mapping to NVIDIA Noble

Bring the address-based I2C ATR implementation and public header from the
working Linux 6.18.48 Yocto integration into NVIDIA's Noble 6.8.12 kernel.
The copied source snapshot in the prepared linux-yocto tree is
a048d872752c64540b4cec640ba7def1860ce460. It includes the published ADI
v18 attach/detach serialization change carried as patch 0013 by this
layer. Keep the original GPL-2.0 identifiers and copyright notices.

Provide dynamic address mapping, static and passthrough flags, private
alias pools and descriptor-based adapter creation required by ADI v18.
Serialize alias attach/detach against transfers across all ATR channels.
Use Noble's master_xfer method and __mutex_init with per-instance lockdep
keys, plus token-valued symbol namespaces, instead of newer interfaces.

Convert all three existing TI consumers rather than disabling them:
DS90UB913 and DS90UB953 use adapter descriptors; DS90UB960 uses address
callbacks and I2C_ATR_F_STATIC to preserve its client-bound alias policy.
Track addresses as address+1 so address zero cannot look like a free slot.
Propagate TI alias-programming failures instead of accepting a broken map.

Keep the temporary alias pointer per call, release fixed aliases after a
partial mapping error, and clear the published adapter pointer if adapter
registration fails. Do not poison later transfers or adapter cleanup.

Rebuild ATR and its TI/ADI consumers together; this changes their internal
kernel API and is not a replacement module for the stock binary kernel.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NVIDIA Noble BSP compatibility backport]

